<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nakhon Si Thammarat</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ligor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nakhon Si Thammarat is a city on the east coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, called Ligor by Europeans. It was the centre of the trading kingdom of Tambralinga and later of a kingdom that spread Sri Lankan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theravada-buddhism">Theravada Buddhism</a> to Sukhothai. Its great stupa, Wat Phra Mahathat, remains one of the most revered in Thailand.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nakhon-si-thammarat.jpg" alt="Nakhon Si Thammarat" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Seksan Phonsuwan · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nai_Mueang,_Mueang_Nakhon_Si_Thammarat_District,_Nakhon_Si_Thammarat_80000,_Thailand_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
